Spec: Select Tool

Purpose:
  Primary interaction tool for selecting, moving, resizing, and rotating shapes.

Owns:
  ./select.ts
  ./select.test.ts

Must:
  Click selects the topmost shape under cursor.
  Click on empty area deselects all.
  Shift+click adds/removes from multi-selection.
  Drag from empty area starts rubber-band selection.
  Right-to-left drag uses crossing selection (partial overlap).
  Left-to-right drag uses enclosing selection (fully inside).
  Drag on selected shape moves all selected shapes.
  Drag resize handles scales selected shapes.
  Drag rotation handle rotates selected shapes around center.
  Snap to grid/endpoints/midpoints when snapping is enabled.
  All moves/resizes/rotations are undoable via commands.

Must not:
  Modify shape data directly — must use MoveShapeCommand, ResizeShapeCommand, RotateShapeCommand.
  Create new shapes.
  Trigger unnecessary re-renders during drag (use restore-from-snapshot pattern).

Depends on:
  @MoveShapeCommand
  @ResizeShapeCommand
  @RotateShapeCommand
  @captureSnapshot
  @restoreSnapshot
  @SnapManager

Scenario: click to select
  Given 2 shapes on canvas and nothing selected
  When the user clicks on shape A
  Then shape A is selected (selectedShapes contains shape A)
  And shape B is not selected

Scenario: click empty area deselects
  Given shape A is selected
  When the user clicks on an empty area of the canvas
  Then no shapes are selected (selectedShapes is empty)

Scenario: shift+click adds to selection
  Given shape A is selected
  When the user Shift+clicks on shape B
  Then both shape A and shape B are selected

Scenario: shift+click removes from selection
  Given shapes A and B are both selected
  When the user Shift+clicks on shape A
  Then only shape B remains selected

Scenario: rubber-band enclosing selection (left-to-right)
  Given 3 shapes on canvas: A and B inside a region, C outside
  When the user drags left-to-right enclosing shapes A and B
  Then shapes A and B are selected
  And shape C (partially outside the rectangle) is not selected

Scenario: rubber-band crossing selection (right-to-left)
  Given 3 shapes on canvas: A fully inside, B partially overlapping
  When the user drags right-to-left over shapes A and B
  Then both A and B are selected (crossing mode includes partial overlap)

Scenario: move shape
  Given shape A is selected at position (100, 100)
  When the user drags shape A by (+100, +100)
  Then shape A's bounding box minX is ~200 and minY is ~200

Scenario: move with undo
  Given shape A is selected at position (100, 100)
  When the user drags shape A to (150, 120)
  Then shape A is at (150, 120)
  When the user presses Ctrl+Z
  Then shape A is back at (100, 100)

Scenario: resize via SE handle
  Given a 100x100 rectangle is selected
  When the user drags the bottom-right handle by (+100, +100)
  Then the shape's width is ~200 and height is ~200

Scenario: resize with undo
  Given a 100x100 rectangle is selected
  When the user resizes it to 200x200 and presses Ctrl+Z
  Then the shape's width returns to ~100

Scenario: rotate shape
  Given a rectangle is selected
  When the user drags the rotation handle
  Then the shape's nodes change position (rotation applied)
  And the operation is undoable with Ctrl+Z

Scenario: keyboard shortcut activates select tool
  Given the Pen tool is active
  When the user presses 'V'
  Then the Select tool becomes active

Tasks:
  [x] Click selection.
  [x] Multi-selection with shift.
  [x] Rubber-band selection (enclosing and crossing).
  [x] Move shapes with snap.
  [x] Resize via 8 handles.
  [x] Rotate via rotation handle.
  [x] Undo/redo for all transforms.
